Wrote the coder-3.json label file. One row for `deportation`: both HB 1393 (2025) passages (authored by Bascom) are coded `v2_relevance: adjacent` — the bill creates a local jail/sheriff notification duty for arrestees with probable unlawful presence, which is an enforcement-cooperation mechanism, not a statement of how far deportation itself should go. No passage survives to support a chair, so `v6_value: null` / `v6_blank_reason: "no-evidence"`, with no quotes extracted.
